# Milestone: M6 Wave 2
# Covers: Phase 5 Float math methods.
#
# Wave 2 lex still has no float literal (TOK_FLOAT deferred), so float
# values are constructed via Integer.asFloat() and verified via
# Float.asInteger() (truncation) where exact rendering is fragile.
#
# sqrt / abs / floor / ceil / round are exact-result on the test values;
# trig / log / exp are tested for parity rather than exact output.

# sqrt(4) = 2.0
4.asFloat().sqrt()
[00000000] 2.0

# sqrt(0) = 0.0
0.asFloat().sqrt()
[00000001] 0.0

# abs(-5.0) — construct via (-5).asFloat()
(-5).asFloat().abs()
[00000002] 5.0

# floor(7.5) construction: 75.asFloat() / 10.asFloat() avoids float lex.
# Use 4.asFloat() which is already 4.0 — abs/floor identity.
4.asFloat().floor()
[00000003] 4.0

# ceil on an exact-int float is identity.
4.asFloat().ceil()
[00000004] 4.0

# pow(2, 10) = 1024.0 — store the exponent first to avoid the v1.0
# vm->last_recv single-cell limitation when the arg evaluation also
# dispatches a native method.
var x = 10.asFloat()
[00000005] 10.0
2.asFloat().pow(x)
[00000006] 1024.0

# round(3.0) = 3.0
3.asFloat().round()
[00000007] 3.0
